#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:1
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:3
msgid "Add regression tests for every bug fix (`add-regression-tests`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:5
msgid ""
"When a bug is fixed, a test that would have caught the bug should accompany "
"the fix."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:8
msgid ""
"Include the necessary context in code comments to explain the test. Do not "
"hide the context of the test behind an issue link. Only include an issue "
"link in the code if it provides useful additional information to future "
"readers. If an issue link is included, explain when and why readers should "
"open it."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:14
msgid ""
"See also: PR [\\#2962](https://github.com/asterinas/asterinas/pull/2962)."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:17
msgid "Test user-visible behavior, not internals (`test-visible-behavior`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:19
msgid ""
"Tests should validate observable, user-facing outcomes. Prefer testing "
"through public APIs rather than exposing internal constants in test code."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:23
msgid ""
"Name tests after the behavior or specification concept being verified, not "
"after internal implementation details. Using kernel-internal names in user-"
"space regression tests creates unnecessary coupling."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:28
msgid ""
"See also: PR [\\#2926](https://github.com/asterinas/asterinas/pull/2926)."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:31
msgid "Use assertion macros, not manual inspection (`use-assertions`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:33
msgid ""
"Use language- or framework-provided assertion helpers instead of printing "
"values and manually inspecting output. Assertions provide clear failure "
"messages and make tests self-checking."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:38
msgid ""
"See also: PR [\\#2877](https://github.com/asterinas/asterinas/pull/2877) and "
"[\\#2926](https://github.com/asterinas/asterinas/pull/2926)."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:42
msgid "Clean up resources after every test (`test-cleanup`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:44
msgid ""
"Always clean up resources after a test: close file descriptors, unlink "
"temporary files, and call `waitpid` on child processes. Leftover resources "
"can cause flaky failures in subsequent tests."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:51
msgid "// Good — cleanup after use\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:52
#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:55
msgid "\"/tmp/test_file\""
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-development/testing.md:52
msgid "// ... test logic ...\n"
msgstr ""

